
<opts>
<isrc>keybd</isrc>
<iname>INPUT</iname>
<iecho>yes</iecho>
<odest>screen</odest>
<oname>home</oname>
<onewl>crlf</onewl>
<scrfont>swiss13</scrfont>
<statwin>on</statwin>
<cfmt>~Piggy contains $%piggy.</cfmt>
<citer>1</citer>
<cdisp>fmtlist</cdisp>
<rtype>fmt</rtype>
<rfmt>\n\N\V</rfmt>
<rall>yes</rall>
<starg></starg>
<srpl></srpl>
<scount>1</scount>
<sout>yes</sout>
<nfmt>fixed</nfmt>
<ndec>2</ndec>
<nang>degrees</nang>
<pltng>off</pltng>
<xmax>5.00</xmax>
<xmin>-5.00</xmin>
<ymax>5.00</ymax>
<ymin>-5.00</ymin>
<xintrvls>5</xintrvls>
<yintrvls>5</yintrvls>
<xycells>home,home</xycells>
<cell>
<cname>dimes</cname>
<text>Enter in the value field the number of dimes in the piggy bank. (Choose Math from the Edit menu or press the Diamond button on S3A to get the math window of this cell.  The value pane is the middle one. If the cursor is not in that pane, you can move it there by pressing TAB).</text>
<val>231</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>half_dollars</cname>
<text>Enter in the value field the number of half dollars in the piggy bank. (Choose Math from the Edit menu or press the Diamond button on S3A to get the math window.  The value field is the middle one).</text>
<val>43</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>home</cname>
<text>The PIGGY web was made for use with the First Tutorial section of the Mathweb Readme.txt file.

Its ostensible purpose is to permit the user to compute the amount of money she has collected in her piggybank, by allowing  entry of the number of pennies, nickles, dimes, quarters, half dollars, and silverdollars; and then to compute the total value of the coinage.

The cells in the web besides "home" are:
    &amp;pennies
    &amp;nickels
    &amp;dimes
    &amp;quarters
    &amp;half_dollars
and
    &amp;silver_dollars

The ampersands (&amp;'s) are not necesary for linking to the other cells.  They are included purely as a convention to denote the names of other cells when they appear in the text area.

The total amount of money in the piggy bank can be computed by evaluating the formula of the cell &amp;piggy.</text></cell>
<cell>
<cname>nickels</cname>
<text>Enter in the value field the number of nickels in the piggy bank. (Choose Math from the Edit menu or press the Diamond button on S3A to get the math window.  The value field is the middle one).</text>
<val>242</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>pennies</cname>
<text>Enter in the value field the number of pennies in the piggy bank. (Choose Math from the Edit menu or press the Diamond button on S3A to get the math window.  The value field is the middle one).</text>
<val>343</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>piggy</cname>
<text>Select Execute from the Special menu to compute the total amount in the piggy bank.</text>
<val>89.13</val>
<script>0.01*pennies+0.05*nickels+0.10*dimes+0.25*quarters+0.50*half_dollars+1.00*silver_dollars</script></cell>
<cell>
<cname>quarters</cname>
<text>Enter in the value field the number of quarters in the piggy bank. (Choose Math from the Edit menu or press the Diamond button on S3A to get the math window.  The value field is the middle one).</text>
<val>100</val></cell>
<cell>
<cname>silver_dollars</cname>
<text>Enter in the value field the number of silver in the piggy bank. (Choose Math from the Edit menu or press the Diamond button on S3A to get the math window.  The value field is the middle one).</text>
<val>4</val></cell></eof>
